# File: tests/features/add_greeting_char_frequency_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/329-add-greeting-char-frequency-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Count each character of the completed greeting

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Count characters of simple and multi-word greetings in first-seen order
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_char_frequency is called with Ada and Ada Lovelace
    Then the results are the exact first-seen-order counts for Hello, Ada and Hello, Ada Lovelace
    And each result is a plain dict

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Keep case and non-ASCII characters distinct without normalization
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_char_frequency is called with Zo plus U+00EB and Zoe plus U+0308
    Then the precomposed result counts U+00EB once and e once
    And the decomposed result counts e twice and U+0308 once with no U+00EB key
    And both results count H once with no h key

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Agree with the existing length and unique-count helpers
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_char_frequency is called with Ada, Ada Lovelace, Agent 007, O'Brien, Zo plus U+00EB, and Ada plus U+674E plus Lee
    Then each result's counts sum to greeting_length of the same name
    And each result has as many keys as greeting_unique_char_count of the same name
    And every count is a positive int

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_char_frequency is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper without changing the CLI
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_char_frequency of Ada
    Then it prints the Ada counts and greeting_char_frequency is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the counting rule and the inherited invalid-name error
    And nmg-smoke Ada still prints exactly Hello, Ada and exits with status 0

